[1424.016, "e\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B  double precision only during\u001b[34Gloading;\u001b[43Gthe\u001b[47Gmain\u001b[52Gcomputation\u001b[64Gstays\u001b[70Gfloat32.\u001b[79GI\u001b[81Gchecked\u001b[89Gthe\u001b[93Gbinary\u001b[100Gand\u001b[104Git\u001b[107Gimports\u001b[115Gno\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B \u001b[5Gmath functions.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B-\u001b[5G\u001b[1mOne token per forward pass.\u001b[22m I did \u001b[40Go\u001b[42G ba\u001b[46Gch prompt tokens \u001b[64Gogether, which would make\u001b[90GFIXED, LOGITS\u001b[104Gand prompt\u001b[K\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1Bprocessing much faster. That\u001b[34Gre\u001b[41G of \"batch\u001b[52Gsize 1, same work\" is stricter than s\u001b[90Grictly necessary, but it's the\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1Bs\u001b[7Gfe\u001b[10Gone.\u001b[K\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1B\u001b[1mNo \u001b[38;2;87;105;247m-ffast-math\u001b[39m.\u001b[22m The compiler's default fused multiply-add\u001b[63Gis on, and that\u001b[79Gisn't\u001b[85Gf\u001b[87Gst-math.\u001b[K\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[1mLimitations\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1B\u001b[22mResults aren't bit-ident\u001b[30Gcal to the reference, because sums are added in a differen\u001b[89G order\u001b[96Gand\u001b[100Gthe\u001b[104Gmath\u001b[109Gfunctions\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1Bare\u001b[9Gmy\u001b[12Gown.\u001b[17GAll\u001b[21Gtop\u001b[25Gtokens\u001b[32Gmatched\u001b[40Gin\u001b[43Gtesting,\u001b[52Gbut\u001b[56Ga\u001b[58Gnear-tie\u001b[67Gin\u001b[70Glogits\u001b[77Gcould\u001b[8"]
